<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_ScaldSteamCarrier.xml              TerminalBiomes
  ==========================================================================
  SCALD_STEAM_WEATHER_DESIGN_1 step 4, built 2026-09-26. The grant half of
  the steam clock: RUT_ScaldExposure does nothing to a pawn who never
  carries it, and this is what puts it on them.

  🔴 WHY THIS IS A SECOND CONDITION AND NOT A FIELD ON THE EXISTING LOCK.
  RUT_ScaldSteamLock uses RM_GameCondition_WeatherPulse, which is what gives
  the Scald its still days; that class has no carrierHediff field, and the
  class that does — GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather — has no periodic
  lapse. Rather than bolt one onto the other (either edit changes shared
  behaviour every other kit depends on), the two run side by side:

    RUT_ScaldSteamLock     forces the weather and pulses the still day
    RUT_ScaldSteamCarrier  grants the exposure hediff, and nothing else

  They cannot fight: this def sets NO forcedWeather, and
  GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather.ForcedWeather() returns exactly
  ext.forcedWeather, i.e. null here (read in full, 2026-09-26) — so the
  pulse lock remains the only thing deciding what the sky is doing.

  Every other field on EnvironmentalWeatherExtension is deliberately unset.
  No damageDef, no hediffToApply, no rot, no plant kill, no temperature
  offset, no density factors: the steam is clean and the WATER is what
  burns (the frozen sheet's own line). This condition's entire job is one
  idempotent hediff grant. damageIntervalTicks is the scan cadence for that
  grant — 2500 ticks, ~1 in-game hour, the same figure RUT_MiasmaWeatherLock
  uses for the same purpose.

  The S7 gate is what makes the Mod Settings toggle real:
  GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather now honours RM_MechanicGateExtension
  (added 2026-09-26, same pattern RM_GameCondition_WeatherPulse already
  had). With S7 off the grant stops, and any exposure already carried heals
  off on its own comp's unexposed rate — nothing is lost and flipping it
  back resumes.
-->
<Defs>

  <GameConditionDef>
    <defName>RUT_ScaldSteamCarrier</defName>
    <conditionClass>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.GameCondition_EnvironmentalWeather</conditionClass>
    <label>standing steam</label>
    <description>The boil's breath stands over everything here. Unroofed, it works on a body the way steam does — and the Scald's own life does not feel it at all.</description>
    <canBePermanent>true</canBePermanent>
    <allowUnderground>true</allowUnderground>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.EnvironmentalWeatherExtension">
        <carrierHediff>RUT_ScaldExposure</carrierHediff>
        <carrierHediffSeverity>0.0001</carrierHediffSeverity>
        <damageIntervalTicks>2500</damageIntervalTicks>
        <affects>Flesh</affects>
        <immuneThingDefs>
          <li>RM_Noohm</li>
          <li>RM_Shulla</li>
          <li>RM_Eesh</li>
          <li>RM_Doss</li>
          <li>RM_Muddal</li>
          <li>RM_Thuum</li>
          <li>RM_Karrash</li>
          <li>RM_Ekkel</li>
          <li>RM_Bladderboil</li>
          <li>RM_ElderSando</li>
        </immuneThingDefs>
      </li>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_MechanicGateExtension">
        <gateKey>Scald.S7</gateKey>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </GameConditionDef>

</Defs>
